    "sections": {
        "description": "<p>Easily embed Booked Scheduler calendars and reservation workflows directly within WordPress using simple Shortcodes.</p>\n<p>This plugin requires a Booked Cloud subscription or a Booked On-Prem installation.</p>\n",
        "installation": "<ol>\n<li>Upload the entire <code>booked</code> directory to the <code>/wp-content/plugins/</code> directory</li>\n<li>Activate the plugin through the &#8216;Plugins&#8217; menu in WordPress</li>\n<li>Update configuration settings from the Booked Scheduler menu item</li>\n<li>Add a Booked Shortcode to any Page or Post</li>\n</ol>\n",
        "faq": "\n<dt id='does%20this%20plugin%20require%20a%20standalone%20booked%20scheduler%20instance%3F'>\nDoes this plugin require a standalone Booked Scheduler instance?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>Yes, this plugin requires a <a href=\"https://www.bookedscheduler.com/free-trial/\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">Booked Cloud</a> subscription or a <a href=\"https://www.bookedscheduler.com/licensing/\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">Booked On-Prem</a> installation.</p>\n</p>\n<dt id='where%20can%20i%20find%20more%20documentation%3F'>\nWhere can I find more documentation?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>Find the latest documentation at <a href=\"https://www.bookedscheduler.com/help/integrations/wordpress\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">Booked Scheduler</a></p>\n</p>\n\n",
        "changelog": "<h4>1.1.0</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Support for event templates</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>1.0.1</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Fix for content auto-sizing</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>1.0.0</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Initial release</li>\n</ul>\n"
    },
